WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.690
In 1990, 1.9 billion people
lived in extreme poverty.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.870
World leaders set eight goals for 2015.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.370
One target: halve the
proportion of people that poor.

4
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.930
By 2015, the number had
fallen to 836 million.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.090
The UN says the target for the
rate was met five years early.

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.630
Then, in 2015, world leaders
agreed a new set of goals.

7
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.730
If the first goals worked, why
did the world need new ones?

8
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.550
In this mission, you'll test the
first goals against their own targets.

9
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll compare the
old goals with the new,

10
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.190
and see what changed between them.

11
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.210
Your mission: explain why the world needed
a new set of goals after halving extreme

12
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.510
poverty early.
